dot/issues/107508","id":3206475643,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6_Hu97","user":{"login":"nstod","id":26262669,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI2MjYyNjY5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/26262669?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nstod","html_url":"https://github.com/nstod","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nstod/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nstod/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nstod/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nstod/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nstod/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nstod/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nstod/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nstod/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nstod/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-20T13:57:19Z","updated_at":"2025-08-20T13:57:19Z","body":"@pennyloafers Yes. Broadcasts work just fine, and as I mentioned in the ticket, you can do multicast on a random port. So network/multicast permissions is not the issue.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3206475643/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3208569884","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/107508#issuecomment-3208569884","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107508","id":3208569884,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6_PuQc","user":{"login":"pennyloafers","id":33847042,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzODQ3MDQy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/33847042?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pennyloafers","html_url":"https://github.com/pennyloafers","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pennyloafers/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pennyloafers/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pennyloafers/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pennyloafers/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pennyloafers/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pennyloafers/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pennyloafers/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pennyloafers/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pennyloafers/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-21T00:50:50Z","updated_at":"2025-08-21T00:50:50Z","body":"I can confirm this functionality works on linux, windows and android from very recent experience using 4.4.1. I also found your reddit thread, to which you said you found the issue with bind and socket option call sequence for the platform. If this has been fixed on your end could you provide some more information on the solution?\n\nI dont have a Mac/iOS to test on, but the only lacking feature i see is leaving the multicast group when the scene exits the tree. I wonder if its possible that the group will throw errors of joined multiple times from the same port and does not clear between runs causing the error.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3208569884/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3208812511","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/107508#issuecomment-3208812511","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107508","id":3208812511,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6_Qpff","user":{"login":"nstod","id":26262669,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI2MjYyNjY5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/26262669?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nstod","html_url":"https://github.com/nstod","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nstod/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nstod/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nstod/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nstod/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nstod/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nstod/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nstod/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nstod/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nstod/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-21T02:45:39Z","updated_at":"2025-08-21T02:45:39Z","body":"I did find the root cause, but I did not fix it, and just changed my game to use broadcast messages (I was trying to search for existing LAN games, and broadcast worked just fine for my needs). I believe the fix will require a change to the API to solve the issue, though. We would need to allow a user to open the socket, join the multicast group, then bind to the port. Because we only have `bind` (which opens and binds) and `join_multicast_group` functions, I believe that's not currently possible. I am not really sure how an API change to fix something like this is handled in this project, especially since it will likely affect all platforms to keep the API in sync.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3208812511/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]